# repos.git — third-party repos cloned into ~/tools/repos (alias-compatible).
# The third-party repos the toolkit's aliases and cheatsheets expect.
# Consumed by modules/80-repos-binaries.sh. The toolkit itself is tools.d/tools.git.
# https throughout: these must clone on a box with no SSH key and no GitHub account.

# --- tunneling / c2 / shells ---
https://github.com/NHAS/reverse_ssh.git
https://github.com/nicocha30/ligolo-ng.git
https://github.com/jpillora/chisel.git
https://github.com/iagox86/dnscat2.git
https://github.com/Mr-Un1k0d3r/SCShell.git

# --- windows / AD offense ---
https://github.com/samratashok/nishang.git
https://github.com/PowerShellMafia/PowerSploit.git
https://github.com/NetSPI/PowerUpSQL.git
https://github.com/GhostPack/Certify.git
https://github.com/NetSPI/ESC.git
https://github.com/dirkjanm/krbrelayx.git
https://github.com/KINGSABRI/MSI-AlwaysInstallElevated.git
https://github.com/Flangvik/SharpCollection.git
https://github.com/ScriptIdiot/SuperSharpShooter.git
https://github.com/tyranid/DotNetToJScript.git
https://github.com/outflanknl/EvilClippy.git

# --- privesc / enum ---
https://github.com/peass-ng/PEASS-ng.git

# --- exploit search ---
# GitLab, not GitHub, and the only non-github.com URL in this file. By far the
# largest clone in it, because it carries the whole Exploit-DB corpus — which is
# the point: searchsploit answers offline, from a network with no egress.
# (The archived github.com/offensive-security/exploitdb mirror is dead; this is
# where Exploit-DB actually publishes.)
https://gitlab.com/exploit-database/exploitdb.git

# --- recon / infra ---
https://github.com/rvrsh3ll/FindFrontableDomains.git
https://github.com/OWASP/joomscan.git

# --- reference / offline cheatsheets (aliases: htricks/gtfo/platt) ---
https://github.com/swisskyrepo/PayloadsAllTheThings.git
https://github.com/swisskyrepo/InternalAllTheThings.git
https://github.com/swisskyrepo/HardwareAllTheThings.git
https://github.com/GTFOBins/GTFOBins.github.io.git
https://github.com/luigigubello/PayloadsAllThePDFs.git
https://github.com/Python-Markdown/markdown.git
